  "name": "Question 7",
  "problem": "Suppose $A$ is a $4\\times 4$ matrix and $det(A)=-63.$ The matrix $B$ is obtained from $A$ by applying the elementary row operation ${R}_{3}:=\\frac{2}{9}{R}_{3}.$ What is the value of $det(B)?$",
  "worked_solution": "The row operation applied to $A$ consists of multiplying a row by the number $\\frac{2}{9}.$\n\nWhen we do this, the determinant is multiplied by the same number. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(B) & =\\frac{2}{9}det(A) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{9}\\cdot (-63) \\\\  & =-14.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
